{"lines": [{"text": "From the start?", "t": 5.54, "end": 6.39}, {"text": "All right.", "t": 7.0, "end": 7.45}, {"text": "A year ago I had forty windows open and couldn't find anything.", "t": 7.948, "end": 11.188}, {"text": "Then I installed a small program called Spaceman.", "t": 11.468, "end": 14.388}, {"text": "It tiles your windows, so they sit side by side and nothing is hidden behind anything else.", "t": 14.748, "end": 19.948}, {"text": "It also gives you numbered workspaces.", "t": 20.268, "end": 22.548}, {"text": "My work went on one and my messages on two.", "t": 22.828, "end": 25.454}, {"text": "I had a camera on my front door, and that's only another window, so I put it on three.", "t": 25.814, "end": 29.916}, {"text": "I found it pleasing.", "t": 30.436, "end": 31.541}, {"text": "So I bought one or two more, and I gave each of my neighbours a workspace of their own.", "t": 37.876, "end": 42.408}, {"text": "Mark is four.", "t": 42.768, "end": 43.808}, {"text": "Joan is five.", "t": 44.128, "end": 45.328}, {"text": "Alan is six.", "t": 45.648, "end": 46.675}, {"text": "I like to know my neighbours.", "t": 47.155, "end": 48.48}, {"text": "Alan's hedge was a little over the limit, so I took a few photographs, for the record.", "t": 51.415, "end": 55.8}, {"text": "And Joan and I disagreed about which day the bins go out.", "t": 61.635, "end": 64.795}, {"text": "I'd kept seven empty, because it's useful to have somewhere to put things.", "t": 69.155, "end": 73.039}, {"text": "I moved Joan there in March, and I've looked after her cat ever since.", "t": 73.399, "end": 77.203}, {"text": "I moved Mark in June.", "t": 79.363, "end": 80.843}, {"text": "Where is Alan now?", "t": 81.978, "end": 83.343, "who": "detective"}, {"text": "He's on seven, with the other two.", "t": 84.188, "end": 86.508}, {"text": "And what is on seven?", "t": 88.143, "end": 89.662, "who": "detective"}, {"text": "Only the one window.", "t": 90.527, "end": 91.807}, {"text": "It's my favourite, I think.", "t": 92.127, "end": 93.529}, {"text": "Everything in it stays exactly where I put it.", "t": 93.889, "end": 96.249}, {"text": "You should try it, Detective.", "t": 98.209, "end": 99.669}, {"text": "You look like a man with a great many windows open.", "t": 100.138, "end": 102.405}], "voice": {"tape": {"stage": "tape", "text": "From the start? All right. A year ago I had forty windows open and couldn't find anything. Then I installed a small program called Spaceman. It tiles your windows, so they sit side by side and nothing is hidden behind anything else. It also gives you numbered workspaces. My work went on one and my messages on two. I had a camera on my front door, and that's only another window, so I put it on three. I found it pleasing. So I bought one or two more, and I gave each of my neighbours a workspace of their own. Mark is four. Joan is five. Alan is six. I like to know my neighbours. Alan's hedge was a little over the limit, so I took a few photographs, for the record. And Joan and I disagreed about which day the bins go out. I'd kept seven empty, because it's useful to have somewhere to put things. I moved Joan there in March, and I've looked after her cat ever since. I moved Mark in June. He's on seven, with the other two. Only the one window. It's my favourite, I think. Everything in it stays exactly where I put it. You should try it, Detective. You look like a man with a great many windows open.", "takes": [{"file": "voice-tape.mp3", "dur": 105.805, "env": [18, 21, 19, 22, 20, 23, 21, 22, 21, 23, 21, 23, 20, 22, 21, 22, 18, 19, 19, 21, 22, 21, 19, 22, 21, 19, 25, 19, 18, 24, 20, 19, 22, 20, 21, 26, 17, 21, 21, 23, 19, 19, 17, 23, 19, 21, 22, 19, 22, 21, 20, 23, 22, 20, 23, 20, 20, 20, 16, 23, 19, 20, 21, 19, 20, 22, 27, 27, 19, 21, 21, 21, 21, 20, 21, 19, 19, 21, 22, 24, 20, 22, 22, 20, 19, 21, 22, 19, 22, 23, 18, 20, 23, 24, 18, 19, 21, 20, 20, 23, 21, 20, 19, 21, 23, 19, 22, 20, 23, 16, 21, 22, 21, 24, 22, 19, 21, 21, 23, 22, 18, 2